00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:24,660
Okay, lesson 13, understanding fair prices and absorption.

22
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:29,060
Fair prices are levels where the market does what it's supposed to do, facilitate trade.

23
00:01:29,060 --> 00:01:32,477
When the market is facilitating trade, both buyers and sellers are happy

24
00:01:32,477 --> 00:01:35,039
to transact at what they deem a fair price.

25
00:01:35,160 --> 00:01:41,920
When you buy a car, you negotiate back and forth with the dealer until you both agree on a fair price.

26
00:01:42,220 --> 00:01:44,240
The same is true in the markets.

27
00:01:44,440 --> 00:01:46,020
Like I said, think about it.

28
00:01:46,060 --> 00:01:49,294
When you go to a car dealership, you have in your mind

29
00:01:49,294 --> 00:01:51,719
what car you want to buy at what price.

30
00:01:51,720 --> 00:01:55,025
The car dealer has in his mind what he wants to sell

31
00:01:55,025 --> 00:01:58,330
that car at, and you guys go back and forth on price

32
00:01:58,330 --> 00:02:01,359
until you both agree at a level that you're happy with.

33
00:02:01,740 --> 00:02:05,116
It may be the car dealer lowers his price and you go

34
00:02:05,116 --> 00:02:07,366
up to it and meet him at that,

35
00:02:07,366 --> 00:02:10,179
or he comes down and meets you at your price.

36
00:02:10,180 --> 00:02:18,440
What you're seeing in the futures markets is just a microcosm of what happens in everyday life.

37
00:02:18,880 --> 00:02:21,920
Absorption will occur at levels of fair prices.

38
00:02:22,320 --> 00:02:29,360
Trade is nearly even distributed between the buyers and seller, with neither side taking control in any discernible way.

39
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:33,575
Now, the easiest way to tell a market is exhibiting absorption is

40
00:02:33,575 --> 00:02:36,385
when there are small deltas in the bar,

41
00:02:36,385 --> 00:02:40,600
when normally you're going to get above average to high delta numbers.

42
00:02:41,160 --> 00:02:47,160
What that means is buyers and sellers are equally matched.

43
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:52,920
Now, consolidation is something that's often confused with absorption.

44
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:57,560
A market can be consolidating, but that doesn't mean it's in absorption.

45
00:02:57,560 --> 00:03:03,280
When a market is consolidating, it's often pending a big move and trading slows down.

46
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:08,620
When a market is in absorption, there can be heavy volume as traders are happy with price and inventory.

47
00:03:09,580 --> 00:03:15,340
So, what I'm trying to say is a market is consolidating. It could be slowing down.

48
00:03:15,680 --> 00:03:18,607
As I said, it could be a number coming out

49
00:03:18,607 --> 00:03:22,119
in an hour, or someone from the Fed could be speaking later.

50
00:03:22,440 --> 00:03:27,760
And the market will generally slow down. You know, volume will contract, it'll get smaller.

51
00:03:28,180 --> 00:03:31,625
Whereas in absorption, price may not be moving, but you're

52
00:03:31,625 --> 00:03:35,759
getting heavy volume trading on both sides. That's one of the differences.

53
00:03:36,260 --> 00:03:40,560
Like I said, even though consolidation, the market's not moving. Absorption, the market's not necessarily moving.

54
00:03:41,040 --> 00:03:43,552
But with absorption, you can get

55
00:03:43,552 --> 00:03:46,902
very heavy volume. And, you know, it's both

56
00:03:46,902 --> 00:03:49,414
buyers and sellers are happy to

57
00:03:49,414 --> 00:03:54,858
move, you know, supply and, you know, move their supply to other buyers.

58
00:03:55,380 --> 00:03:58,127
So, a market can range trade during and after absorption,

59
00:03:58,127 --> 00:04:01,699
