00:37:06,240 --> 00:37:09,480
And then you just see it sort of goes sideways with some fairly small deltas.

692
00:37:09,560 --> 00:37:11,020
And you see the buying really appear.

693
00:37:11,640 --> 00:37:13,080
You know, this bar here with

694
00:37:13,080 --> 00:37:14,280
a negative delta of 1,300, it

695
00:37:14,280 --> 00:37:16,680
was probably more at one point. It was probably minus 2,000.

696
00:37:17,240 --> 00:37:20,280
But the buying came in late to push it higher.

697
00:37:20,700 --> 00:37:26,830
And then the next bar just sort of goes sideways, you know, sideways to higher.

698
00:37:26,830 --> 00:37:29,630
And then you see the market start to move away.

699
00:37:29,710 --> 00:37:33,610
But it's moving away on strong deltas, 900, 700, 500, 2,000.

700
00:37:38,240 --> 00:37:39,220
Here's an ES chart.

701
00:37:40,440 --> 00:37:41,200
And what happens?

702
00:37:41,300 --> 00:37:42,410
You come up here, you hit

703
00:37:42,410 --> 00:37:43,520
the high, you got a delta

704
00:37:43,520 --> 00:37:46,852
of 2. You know, as you're sort of going up there, it kind of stalled out a little bit.

705
00:37:47,080 --> 00:37:54,060
You know, you got this delta of 562. You know, it's kind of, you know, it's very a neutral number.

706
00:37:54,940 --> 00:37:56,000
You get a final push here.

707
00:37:56,080 --> 00:37:57,820
You're thinking, okay, now the buying's coming back.

708
00:37:57,900 --> 00:38:03,480
But then you hit the high and you got a delta of 2. You know, 16,000 lots traded in this bar.

709
00:38:03,600 --> 00:38:04,680
It's got a delta of 2.

710
00:38:05,480 --> 00:38:06,800
Where's the follow-through buying?

711
00:38:06,940 --> 00:38:08,625
You know, if you're looking for the

712
00:38:08,625 --> 00:38:10,310
market to keep going up, you know,

713
00:38:10,310 --> 00:38:12,958
especially after this bar with some strong positive delta, it didn't.

714
00:38:13,100 --> 00:38:14,260
You know, there was no follow-through.

715
00:38:14,260 --> 00:38:16,068
And, you know, where you had a

716
00:38:16,068 --> 00:38:17,618
lot of demand on this move

717
00:38:17,618 --> 00:38:20,718
up, all of a sudden now you've got a lot of supply.

718
00:38:21,180 --> 00:38:24,080
Then the next bar, very strong negative delta, 2,000.

719
00:38:24,360 --> 00:38:25,640
Here you got the single print.

720
00:38:27,140 --> 00:38:29,104
You know, it was a nice little

721
00:38:29,104 --> 00:38:30,788
trade you could have taken in

722
00:38:30,788 --> 00:38:32,191
this bar, I think, here

723
00:38:32,191 --> 00:38:34,997
at 957 to get, you know, get a nice little profit.

724
00:38:39,500 --> 00:38:42,020
E-minis, again, you know, what's happening?

725
00:38:42,020 --> 00:38:50,840
You get 30, 127, 200, 300, 400, 200. Yeah, these are all relatively small delta numbers.

726
00:38:51,220 --> 00:38:56,300
You know, I mean, you know, 200, 300, 400 is kind of, you know, just a little bit outside of the band.

727
00:38:56,440 --> 00:38:57,668
You know, definitely if

728
00:38:57,668 --> 00:38:59,203
I see a number around 150

729
00:38:59,203 --> 00:39:01,046
to 100 and lower, it's kind of,

730
00:39:01,046 --> 00:39:02,581
you know, neutral in the

731
00:39:02,581 --> 00:39:07,803
sense that, you know, one trade can be the difference of this delta being positive or negative.

732
00:39:08,620 --> 00:39:11,960
You know, 200, 300, 400 is probably a difference of two trades.

733
00:39:12,840 --> 00:39:15,720
But, you know, what's happening?

734
00:39:16,120 --> 00:39:19,820
You know, it's kind of evenly distributed, a little bit more to the negative side.

735
00:39:20,200 --> 00:39:21,840
But we're up here near the high.

736
00:39:21,980 --> 00:39:24,400
So you're seeing, again, you know, is it absorption?

737
00:39:24,600 --> 00:39:26,000
You know, yeah, people are happy to trade.

738
00:39:26,100 --> 00:39:29,280
You know, buyers, there is demand to sort of move it higher, but it's met with sellers.

739
00:39:31,610 --> 00:39:32,730
And then the selling comes in.

740
00:39:32,810 --> 00:39:33,710
The sellers take over.

741
00:39:33,990 --> 00:39:37,770
You know, people that, you know, the demand that was there isn't necessarily there, but the supply is there.

742
00:39:37,770 --> 00:39:39,110
The supply is moving.

743
00:39:39,110 --> 00:39:43,630
And the price is lower as the people that own the supply are looking to get rid of it.

744
00:39:47,080 --> 00:39:48,760
And, you know, lastly is the 10-year chart.

745
00:39:48,880 --> 00:39:51,260
You know, 10 years are a very liquid market.

746
00:39:51,740 --> 00:39:54,440
And, you know, you're going to see big numbers in the volume profile.

747
00:39:54,440 --> 00:39:57,680
So when you see small numbers in the deltas, you know, watch out.

748
00:39:58,320 --> 00:40:02,820
And, you know, here's a bar that's traded 5,000.

749
00:40:02,900 --> 00:40:04,300
You've got a delta of 41.

750
00:40:04,520 --> 00:40:05,900
Here's a bar that's traded 10,000.

751
00:40:05,980 --> 00:40:08,420
You've got a delta of 159.

752
00:40:09,720 --> 00:40:11,340
You know, those are very small deltas.

753
00:40:11,440 --> 00:40:14,700
And usually on a 10-year chart, you're going to see deltas in a couple of thousands.

754
00:40:15,540 --> 00:40:16,780
And, you know, what's happening?

755
00:40:16,860 --> 00:40:21,320
You've sort of come down into this low area, and you're sort of going sideways.

756
00:40:21,320 --> 00:40:23,700
You can see the point of control is all sort of lining up here.

757
00:40:24,320 --> 00:40:27,260
And the deltas are fairly small, 41, 159.

758
00:40:27,440 --> 00:40:33,380
But, you know what? It's sandwiched around these deltas here, 1,300, 2,700.

759
00:40:34,240 --> 00:40:36,120
But what's happening?

760
00:40:36,660 --> 00:40:41,460
You know, you're at a low, and you're seeing buying takeover from earlier on the move down.

761
00:40:41,540 --> 00:40:42,680
You're seeing the selling takeover.

762
00:40:43,000 --> 00:40:44,780
So, you know, watch it.

763
00:40:44,880 --> 00:40:46,070
Is it, you know, this

764
00:40:46,070 --> 00:40:47,737
is an area where, you know, coming

765
00:40:47,737 --> 00:40:49,404
into here, you don't know if it's

766
00:40:49,404 --> 00:40:52,738
going to keep going lower or stop and then turn around and go up.

767
00:40:53,280 --> 00:40:56,880
That's an area where there's, you know, I'll say fair trade.

768
00:40:57,020 --> 00:40:59,800
But, you know, buyers and sellers are evenly matched for the most part.

769
00:41:00,100 --> 00:41:04,820
And you're seeing a shift in supply and demand.

770
00:41:04,920 --> 00:41:07,540
Now, you're seeing demand takeover as the market starts to go up.

771
00:41:07,640 --> 00:41:11,040
You know, and really your clue in that shift is the delta.

772
00:41:11,720 --> 00:41:14,540
You know, whereas before you're seeing strong negative deltas on the way down.

773
00:41:14,540 --> 00:41:17,720
Now, you're starting to see you're at the low deltas sort of go flat.

774
00:41:18,420 --> 00:41:20,220
And you're starting to build up positive.

775
00:41:20,340 --> 00:41:21,800
You're seeing the demand pick up.

776
00:41:23,100 --> 00:41:26,960
You know, I mean, people looking at bar charts will say, oh, you know, you can see that.

777
00:41:27,300 --> 00:41:28,600
Supply and shift in supply and demand.

778
00:41:28,780 --> 00:41:29,520
Well, you know, can you?

779
00:41:29,580 --> 00:41:32,820
Why didn't it happen here in this bar, you know, where you had it earlier?

780
00:41:32,900 --> 00:41:34,340
But you see when, you know,

781
00:41:34,340 --> 00:41:35,780
the buying and selling are evenly

782
00:41:35,780 --> 00:41:36,980
matched. You know, people are

783
00:41:36,980 --> 00:41:41,540
happy with the price here. You know, it's a fair price. Prices are happy to trade at these levels.

784
00:41:42,140 --> 00:41:47,540
And then, you know, price just sort of starts ticking back up on more demand.

785
00:41:49,860 --> 00:41:54,080
So, you know, the main thing in this chapter was understanding fair prices and absorption.

786
00:41:55,300 --> 00:42:01,160
I hate to use consolidation because consolidation, markets consolidate all the times and it's due to external factors.

787
00:42:01,560 --> 00:42:03,800
Whereas absorption happens because, you know, market

788
00:42:03,800 --> 00:42:06,360
reaches price level where people are happy to

789
00:42:06,360 --> 00:42:11,160
trade. And you see a lot of volume sometimes go through without moving the price.

790
00:42:11,540 --> 00:42:13,760
So, you know, people that have size

791
00:42:13,760 --> 00:42:16,297
to move in the market, they want to

792
00:42:16,297 --> 00:42:18,517
trade at times of days when they

793
00:42:18,517 --> 00:42:25,178
can move their size, you know, without moving the market. You know, whether it's, you know, cash open, the cash closed.

794
00:42:25,180 --> 00:42:27,669
So, even during the day when we reach

795
00:42:27,669 --> 00:42:29,847
certain price levels, maybe it could be

796
00:42:29,847 --> 00:42:32,959
support or resistance, you know, the reason doesn't necessarily matter.

797
00:42:33,560 --> 00:42:36,614
But what you want to know is you want to

798
00:42:36,614 --> 00:42:39,668
see where, you know, price reaches a level where buyers

799
00:42:39,668 --> 00:42:46,998
and sellers come in on both sides and are evenly matched. And then what happens as you start to move out of that area.

800
00:42:49,570 --> 00:42:53,010
So, that's the end of Lesson 13, Fair Prices and Absorption.

801
00:42:53,010 --> 00:42:57,210
And in the next lesson, I'll show you how to read the market using order flow.

802
00:42:57,350 --> 00:42:59,894
I mean, I sort of touched on

803
00:42:59,894 --> 00:43:02,438
it a bit, you know, in this

804
00:43:02,438 --> 00:43:07,889
chapter, starting to put things together with Delta and, you know, price rejection, single prints.

805
00:43:08,450 --> 00:43:10,169
But, you know, really once

806
00:43:10,169 --> 00:43:12,575
you really understand order flow, reading the

807
00:43:12,575 --> 00:43:15,669
market is just like reading a book, you know.

808
00:43:15,670 --> 00:43:17,539
And I think one of the reasons why

809
00:43:17,539 --> 00:43:19,408
people get discouraged with order flow is they

810
00:43:19,408 --> 00:43:21,277
see a lot of numbers and they just,

811
00:43:21,277 --> 00:43:25,949
you know, think, oh, you know, my head is going to explode with all those numbers. I don't understand math.

812
00:43:26,030 --> 00:43:28,490
And you don't need to know math with order flow.

813
00:43:29,150 --> 00:43:33,690
You know, you just need to understand, you know, just the basic supply and demand and go from there.

814
00:43:35,170 --> 00:43:35,950
So, thank you.

815
00:43:36,010 --> 00:43:37,150
That's the end of Lesson 13.

816
00:43:37,150 --> 00:44:07,130
So, thank you.

